    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0092" n="80" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg80"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.8411/11–2944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-29T22:00:00+03:00">November 29,
                            1944—10 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 29—3:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>248. Re Legation’s 245, November 27. Acceptance by Emperor this evening of
                    British formula in which Ethiopia as contribution of ally to prosecution of war
                    places reserved areas and Ogaden under administration <pb facs="0093" n="81"
                        xml:id="pg81"/> of British military for life of agreement ensures resumption
                    of negotiations and makes possible successful conclusion. Copies of documents in
                    pouch on tomorrow morning’s plane.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d73-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
